figdown 0.1 table
# `RULE-POSITION-ENUMERATION`: RULE 2.4's COMPLEMENT, and it is what stops 2.3 and 2.4
# disagreeing at the table `width` position. Where a value comes from an OPEN
# VALUE SPACE — a number, a point, a percentage, a range — redundant quotes
# are INERT and legal: the model below is byte-identical to the one the bare
# spellings produce. `index=`'s inertness is normative and load-bearing here
# (core §12.7, §9 `INDEX-RANGE-STEP`).
# `auto` and `*` are the two WORD-shaped spellings inside otherwise-numeric
# grammars; they stay inert deliberately, SYNTAX-STYLE §8.6.
table t "T"
| A | B |
|---|---|
| 1 | 2 |
width "auto",90
cell "(1,1)" fill=#fee2e2
figdown 0.1 bitfield
bitfield bf "H" numbering=msb0
field "A" "8"
field "B" 8 index="0..7"
field "C" "*"
figdown 0.1 block
node n1 "N1"
group g "G" gap="4"
layout
pin n1 at="(40,40)" width="90"
